---
title: "Cluster"
description: "Lays children out in a row that wraps onto new lines, with even gaps."
tags: [layout, css]
usage: |
  Add the `cluster` class to a container. Good for tags, button groups and
  toolbars. Adjust it with the custom properties below, either in a stylesheet or
  inline with `style`.
customProperties:
  "--cluster-align": "Vertical alignment of the items (`align-items`)."
  "--cluster-justify": "Horizontal distribution of the items (`justify-content`)."
  "--cluster-space": "Gap between items, in both directions."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<div class="cluster" style="--cluster-space: 0.5rem">
  <span>One</span>
  <span>Two</span>
  <span>Three</span>
  <span>Four</span>
</div>
